    },
    "body": "Multi-source reads had weak query-to-source binding even after frozen-context readout learning. This adds a stable text-cue carrier, independently encoded query geometry, and a learned directed signed-H4 q4 contribution to every admitted Copy occurrence before the existing global Copy/Period/Stop alias reduction. Parent weights remain frozen; native generation loads packed cue weights without the offline F32 shadow. A cue-unary interaction ablation and prospective fresh-only panel preparation are included.\n\nAt the exact scientific source d2a899271e4a41abf916120f104b2be6bc626885, both CPU-only Rust fits complete 64 balanced B8 updates and select checkpoint 48. Directed development CE improves 1.1461994784→1.0400545984; cue-unary reaches 1.1242191199. All 34/64 uncued complete answers remain unchanged. Development banks are 2/64 versus 1/64; fresh complete answers are 0/32 versus 1/32, with no complete query pair. These results establish learned native cue influence, not reliable geometric attention or a geometric advantage.\n\nValidation: four distinct integer cue tests, three offline cue tests, two existing bank-loss regressions, twelve driver tests, seven panel tests and release builds pass. The extra angular command repeats an integer test. Exact-source delivery and both complete returned result sets are verified by SHA256 and full file set. Independent saved-evidence audits reconstruct all F32/q4 exports and native alias arithmetic; they do not rerun BPE, backward computation or native inference. Linux Metal checks are unavailable. No GitHub research runner, GPU, shared session/compiler edit or default promotion.\n\nThe next causal seam is learned ordered source-prefix/actual-response-prefix transport: useful role association still selects internal token offsets and loops. Retain all gains, regressions and candidates; no unchanged dose or authored cursor.\n\nReferences #1552 and #820.\n",
